<main class="lux-article-page"><nav class="lux-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="<?php echo esc_url(luxureat_static_url('en', '')); ?>">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><a href="<?php echo esc_url(luxureat_static_url('en/recipe', '')); ?>">Recipes</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Creamy Mushroom Soup</span></nav><article class="lux-recipe-reader lux-recipe-seo-page"><section class="lux-recipe-hero"><figure><img width="1000" height="667" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" src="<?php echo esc_url(get_template_directory_uri() . '/assets/media/journal/recipe-mushroom-soup.webp'); ?>" alt="Creamy Mushroom Soup"></figure><div class="lux-recipe-intro"><span>First Courses</span><h1 id="lux-reader-title">Creamy Mushroom Soup</h1><p>A warm and comforting first course for autumn. This silky mushroom soup carries deep woodland aromas and is especially good with golden croutons or a drizzle of truffle oil.</p><dl class="lux-recipe-facts"><div><dt>Time</dt><dd>35 min</dd></div><div><dt>Difficulty</dt><dd>Easy</dd></div><div><dt>Serves</dt><dd>2 servings</dd></div></dl></div></section><section class="lux-recipe-body"><aside class="lux-recipe-ingredients"><h2>Ingredients</h2><ul><li>300 g mixed fresh mushrooms, such as shiitake, porcini, or button mushrooms</li><li>1 medium potato</li><li>½ onion</li><li>1 garlic clove</li><li>2 tablespoons extra-virgin olive oil</li><li>400 ml hot vegetable stock</li><li>2 tablespoons fresh cream (optional)</li><li>Salt and pepper, to taste</li><li>Fresh chopped parsley, to garnish</li><li>Croutons, to serve</li></ul></aside><div class="lux-recipe-method"><h2>Method</h2><ol><li>Wipe the mushrooms with a damp cloth and slice them. Peel and dice the potato; finely chop the onion and garlic.</li><li>Heat the olive oil and sauté the onion and garlic for 2–3 minutes. Add the mushrooms and potato and cook for about 5 minutes.</li><li>Pour in the hot vegetable stock, cover, and simmer over medium heat for about 20 minutes, until tender.</li><li>Remove from the heat and blend until smooth. Stir in the cream for a richer texture, if desired.</li><li>Season with salt and pepper, garnish with parsley, and serve hot with golden croutons or a drizzle of truffle oil.</li></ol></div></section><section class="lux-recipe-nutrition"><header><h2>Estimated nutrition per serving</h2></header><dl><div><dt>Energy</dt><dd>870 kJ (about 210 kcal)</dd></div><div><dt>Saturated fat</dt><dd>2 g (10%)</dd></div><div><dt>Carbohydrates (sugars)</dt><dd>14 g (including 4 g sugars)</dd></div><div><dt>Protein</dt><dd>6 g</dd></div></dl></section><section class="lux-recipe-details"><div><dt>Reference region</dt><dd>Reference: Umbrian / Central Italian style</dd></div><div><dt>Suggested oil</dt><dd>A gently fruity extra-virgin olive oil</dd></div><div><dt>Allergen note</dt><dd>Contains milk if cream is used; check the stock label</dd></div><div><dt>Substitutions</dt><dd>Omit cream or use unsweetened oat milk; mushrooms can follow local supply</dd></div><div><dt>Related products</dt><dd><a class="lux-recipe-product-link" href="<?php echo esc_url(luxureat_static_url('en/product', '?category=truffle#product-catalogue')); ?>">Truffle catalogue (subject to live stock and label)</a></dd></div></section></article></main>
